{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>בֵּן פֹּרָת יוֹסֵף בֵּן פֹּרָת עֲלֵי עָיִן.</b> Jacob said that Joseph, on his own account, is בֵּן פֹּרָת — in the sense of פְּרִיָּה וּרְבִיָּה, for Joseph is the language of increase, as in ״יוֹסֵף עֲלֵיכֶם כָּכֶם אֶלֶף פְּעָמִים״ (Deuteronomy 1:11). And he said ״בֵּן פֹּרָת עֲלֵי עָיִן״ — because he is a master of grace, on the model of what is said (Esther 2:15) ״נוֹשֵׂאת חֵן בְּעֵינֵי כָּל רֹאֶיהָ״; therefore he will be עֲלֵי עָיִן, for the evil eye has no dominion over one who bears grace in the eyes of all who see him. And the proof of this is that ״בָּנוֹת צָעֲדָה עֲלֵי שׁוּר״ — to gaze at his beauty, and even so he was not harmed by the evil eye, even though in a place where abundance is found, there the evil eye is found even more; nevertheless Joseph is בֶּן פֹּרָת, that he will be fruitful and multiply like those fish, and even so his charm will be bent over the eye of the beholder, so as not to harm him." "And after he mentioned the harm of the evil eye of all who saw him, from which he escaped, he returned to mention a second matter similar to it: for his brothers too were jealous of him and cast their eyes upon him, and he escaped from them as well. And this is what it says: ״וַיְמָרֲרֻהוּ וָרֹבּוּ וַיִּשְׂטְמֻהוּ בַּעֲלֵי חִצִּים״ (Genesis 49:23). And the matter of ״וָרֹבּוּ״ is like ״רֹבֶה קַשָּׁת״, for they sought to kill him by means of an arrow, as it says ״וּבְטֶרֶם יִקְרַב אֲלֵיהֶם וַיִּתְנַכְּלוּ אֹתוֹ לַהֲמִיתוֹ״ (Genesis 37:18), and that is by means of an arrow — because they considered him a slanderer, for ״חֵץ שָׁחוּט לְשׁוֹנוֹ״ (Jeremiah 9:7); therefore they sought to do to him measure for measure. ״וַיִּשְׂטְמֻהוּ בַּעֲלֵי חִצִּים״ — they themselves were בַּעֲלֵי חִצִּים whose ״חֵץ שָׁחוּט לְשׁוֹנָם״, for they themselves had brought slander against the sons of the maidservants, calling them slaves; ״וַיָּבֵא יוֹסֵף אֶת דִּבָּתָם רָעָה״ (Genesis 37:2) — that they had brought slander against the sons of Bilhah and Zilpah to their father. Therefore ״וַתֵּשֶׁב בְּאֵיתָן קַשְׁתּוֹ״ (Genesis 49:24) — the bow of Joseph, for it is permitted to speak lashon ha-ra about instigators of conflict (Jerusalem Pe'ah 1:1). And according to this, the bow of Joseph shot according to law, but the brothers are fit to be called בַּעֲלֵי חִצִּים, and the arrows of Joseph descended upon them in judgment. ״וַיָּפֹזּוּ זְרֹעֵי יָדָיו״ (Genesis 49:24), for ״רֹעֶה זוֹנוֹת יְאַבֶּד הוֹן״ (Proverbs 29:3), and he was not a רֹעֶה זוֹנוֹת with the wife of Potiphar; therefore he merited vast wealth and merited to be רֹעֶה אֶבֶן יִשְׂרָאֵל."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:34:47.059234608Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}